      "content": "I'm not asking you to fake any data or lie about the numbers themselves. I'm just saying the reviewers are going to be looking for any reason to reject this, and a \"p=0.06\" can sometimes come across as a non-result if it's phrased too dryly. \n\nI need you to frame the findings in a way that shows the potential of the data. How can we describe the statistical strength of the Protein-X correlation so it emphasizes the trend and the scientific importance without actually changing the raw p-value?",
